# Testing Time Budget

The testing/QA phase for any feature work in this repository **must complete within 30 minutes** of wall-clock time.

## Rule

- All tests + smoke checks + manual verification steps for a single bug fix or feature MUST fit inside a **30-minute** testing window.
- When 30 minutes is reached, stop expanding coverage. Ship what passed, log what didn't, and surface the gap to the user.
- Do not invent new test cases once the budget is exhausted — every additional case compounds the time-cost.
- Run tests in parallel where the harness supports it (Vitest `--reporter=basic --maxConcurrency`, Playwright workers).

## Why

- Production bug-fix velocity > exhaustive coverage.
- The team triages gaps weekly, so unreached cases surface naturally.
- Avoids the "test the tests" anti-pattern.

## What counts as testing

- Unit + integration tests under `tests/unit/`.
- E2E specs under `tests/e2e/` and `tests/automation/Playwright/specs/`.
- Manual smoke checks via `npm run build` / `npm run dev` / browser screenshots.
- Lint, type-check (`npx tsc --noEmit`), and Prettier dry-runs.

## What doesn't count

- Reading source to scope the fix.
- Implementing the fix itself.
- Commit / push / Vercel preview verification (those are deployment, not testing).
